Part A: members of length <= L, against C*L^a* (strict form needs count <= C*t(L) for all large L).
set                           C  a*  least L with count > C L^a*    count there
Craig, fast f                 1   3                         1113      1.611e+09
Craig, fast f                 1   5                         3962      1.153e+18
Craig, fast f           1000000   3                         3425      5.404e+16
Craig, fast f           1000000   5                         7674      2.901e+25
{R(w) -> R(w)}                1   3                           39      6.553e+04
{R(w) -> R(w)}                1   5                           69      2.147e+09
{R(w) -> R(w)}          1000000   3                           87      1.100e+12
{R(w) -> R(w)}          1000000   5                          117      3.603e+16
Pad(q) (Lemma 2.1): at most L members of length <= L for every L (one per counter value T, length >= T+1),
  so it never exceeds C L^a* with C >= 1.
  -> no enumerator of the fast Craig set or of the template {R(w) -> R(w)} meets the strict form, whatever
     its order; P2-strict admits only sparse sets (Pad(q) among them) and excludes every schema.

